 southeastern corner of the Adriatic Sea. Durrës's climate is profoundly influenced by a seasonal Mediterranean climate.", "newValue": "Durrës, located on the Adriatic coast of Albania, is one of the oldest continuously inhabited cities in the world, with its origins tracing back to the 7th century BCE when it was founded by the Illyrians. This city has served as a vital port and trade hub throughout its history, strategically positioned between the western Mediterranean and the Balkans. Durrës played a significant role during the Roman Empire, becoming a key naval base known as Dyrrhachium, where it served as a gateway for military expeditions and trade routes connecting the east to the west.

